# claude-settings.json.schema
#
# Companion document for `claude-settings.json`, the Claude harness's
# configuration template. The build substitutes the `@…@` placeholders and
# writes the result to `<P-9 HARNESS_HOME>/settings.json`, which is the file this
# CLI reads (see `modules/router-wiring.md`).
#
# ## Every key, and why it is here
#
# | Key | Parameter | Effect |
# |---|---|---|
# | `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` | `P-3` | Routes requests to the router instead of the first-party endpoint. |
# | `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | `P-5` | The model the session uses — an alias from the router's set. |
# | `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL` | `P-6` | What the CLI's small/fast role resolves to: background work and session titles. The older `ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL` name is deprecated. |
# | `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS` | `P-7` | The context window the CLI assumes for the active model. It exists for exactly this case: a model reached through `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` whose window does not match the CLI's built-in size for its name, which is every alias. |
# | `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` | `P-8` | The maximum output tokens for most requests. |
#
# ## What must not be in this file
#
# The credential. This `env` block sets **values**, so a credential written here
# would be a credential in an image layer — in every container started from it,
# and in every copy of the image (R-8). The deployment injects
# `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` into the process environment instead, and the CLI sends
# it as `Authorization: Bearer <value>`. Do not name `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in its
# place: that variable sets a different header (`X-Api-Key`), which the router
# does not read.
#
# Nor a second provider: no fallback endpoint, no direct first-party URL for a
# role the router serves (R-7). Every route in this file goes through `P-3`.
#
# ## Validation
#
# ```
# docker run --rm --entrypoint sh <image> -c 'cat "${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR}/settings.json"'
# docker run --rm --entrypoint sh <image> -c 'jq -r .env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL "${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR}/settings.json"'
# ```
#
# The file must parse as JSON, contain no `@…@` placeholder, and carry no
# credential-shaped string — an `sk-`, `Bearer `, or a token of any kind.
